From a93f3548feabb683b4f768f17cae216265aa30de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael John <mj@tierone.software>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 18:37:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] stat/sort: bound two unbounded stack writes (argv-only,
 hardening)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

stat format1(): lfmt[24] can receive up to 31 bytes of assembled
printf format ('%' + 5 flag chars + 10-digit size + 11-char precision
+ 'll' + conversion + NUL) — stat -f '%# +-02147483647.2147483647z'
aborts fortify builds.  Widen lfmt to 64; every component was already
individually bounded, no logic change.

sort parse_pos_obs(): the obsolete +POS syntax's option-letter run is
strncpy'd into the caller's 128-byte stack buffer with no length check
(sort +1.0<300 letters> smashes the frame; fortify abort).  Reject
over-long runs (parse fails, arg left untouched — the existing error
idiom); this also secures the sopt[304] sprintfs whose sizing assumes
sopts <= 127.  Legitimate obsolete keys (+1.0n etc.) still work.

Both self-inflicted (argv-only); both verbatim upstream FreeBSD.
PoC-verified pre/post.  Upstream patch queued as
upstream-patches/0049.
---
 src.freebsd/coreutils/sort/sort.c | 4 ++++
 src.freebsd/coreutils/stat/stat.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src.freebsd/coreutils/sort/sort.c b/src.freebsd/coreutils/sort/sort.c
index cb8fe882e..b1704cb3e 100644
--- a/src.freebsd/coreutils/sort/sort.c
+++ b/src.freebsd/coreutils/sort/sort.c
@@ -846,6 +846,10 @@ parse_pos_obs(const char *s, int *nf, int *nc, char* sopts)
 
 		len = pmatch[3].rm_eo - pmatch[3].rm_so;
 
+		/* sopts is a 128-byte buffer at both call sites */
+		if (len >= 128)
+			goto end;
+
 		strncpy(sopts, s + pmatch[3].rm_so, len);
 		sopts[len] = '\0';
 	}
diff --git a/src.freebsd/coreutils/stat/stat.c b/src.freebsd/coreutils/stat/stat.c
index 548d96eaf..2f725d127 100644
--- a/src.freebsd/coreutils/stat/stat.c
+++ b/src.freebsd/coreutils/stat/stat.c
@@ -614,7 +614,7 @@ format1(const struct stat *st,
     int hilo, int what)
 {
 	u_int64_t data;
-	char *stmp, lfmt[24], tmp[20];
+	char *stmp, lfmt[64], tmp[20];
 	struct passwd *pw = NULL;
 	struct group *gr = NULL;
 	const char *sdata = NULL;
-- 
2.43.0

